From 6d66d3ab7c8218ee0bc70cf0bb75feac702878e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LadyHwesta <tiesa@meskis.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:51:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Automate dedicated-VPS creation via UpCloud's API

Direct follow-up to the deployment-agent work: "for customers that
will have their own private vps, I just created an API key on
UpCloud. Can we automate the deployment of the initial VPS server this
way?" Closes the one prerequisite the bootstrap script itself can't -
the box existing at all - without changing the earlier decision that
the bootstrap script itself still runs by hand, by Tiesa, never the
customer.

- upcloud_client.py: thin UpCloudClient (create/get/stop/delete
  server, list zones/plans), same shape as every other API client in
  this repo.
- upcloud_account.py: upcloud.account holds the API token, Tiesa's own
  SSH public key (injected into every new server so she can run the
  bootstrap script afterward), and zone/plan/OS-template defaults.
  System group only - not even plain internal users can read it,
  since a compromised token can spend real money broadly.
- deployment.server gains vps_provider/upcloud_account_id/upcloud_uuid/
  upcloud_state fields and three actions (Create UpCloud Server, Check
  VPS Status, Destroy VPS). action_request()'s generated checklist
  gains one more task, "Create the UpCloud VPS," ahead of "Confirm
  server access," when applicable.

**Live-verified 2026-09-15** against the user's real UpCloud account -
created a real STARTER-1xCPU-1GB server from the Debian 12 template,
confirmed SSH login with the injected key actually worked, then
stopped and deleted it (confirmed gone via a follow-up 404). Two real
findings baked into the client:
- `metadata` in the create-server body must be the literal string
  "yes", not a JSON boolean - `true` is rejected outright
  (METADATA_INVALID), needed at all because cloning a cloud-init-based
  template (the standard Debian/Ubuntu ones) fails otherwise
  (METADATA_DISABLED_ON_CLOUD-INIT).
- Reaching state "started" does NOT mean SSH is actually reachable yet
  - a real connection got refused immediately after "started", only
  succeeding ~15s later. UpCloudClient.wait_for_state() and the
  Check VPS Status notification both account for this.

Also fixed a real design gap this surfaced: deployment.server's own
hostname/agent_url were required=True, but neither is actually known
at creation time for an UpCloud-provisioned server (the IP doesn't
exist until Create UpCloud Server runs, the agent isn't installed
until the bootstrap script runs after that). Both relaxed to optional,
with _get_client() raising a clear guard instead of relying on a DB
constraint.

329 tests green across the full 12-module regression suite (41 in
this module alone, up from 24).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
